1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,565
Khonsu Moonlight
A real coding session in the local 0.7.0 build. Synthetic example code.

2
00:00:03,565 --> 00:00:18,460
Write. Correct. Format.
Typing paced to about 130 WPM. Fix the condition, then let Prettier format on save.

3
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:31,086
Code you can read
Python syntax colours, softer interface text and a matching integrated terminal.

4
00:00:31,086 --> 00:00:45,179
Choose your tools
Preview the optional extension catalogue. Nothing is installed in this step.

5
00:00:45,179 --> 00:00:56,121
Settings you can undo
Apply the appearance preset, then restore the previous values.

6
00:00:56,121 --> 00:01:12,920
Make room for focus
Start a 25-minute session. Pause and resume from the status bar.

7
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:27,621
Take a pet break
Pet, carry, flick the ball and tap the cushion. System reduced motion is respected.

8
00:01:27,621 --> 00:01:42,987
Meet Pixel
Choose a Labrador, give it a name and pick a colour. Then play directly in the scene.

9
00:01:42,987 --> 00:02:15,862
Motion-enabled pet preview
Separate local production-webview fixture capture, CUA screenshot sequence. No OS preference was changed.

10
00:02:15,862 --> 00:02:22,673
Back to work
Hide the pet without losing it. Stop the focus session when you are done.

11
00:02:22,673 --> 00:02:27,323
Vim or Neovim
Preview the optional backend choices. No backend is installed or changed here.

12
00:02:27,323 --> 00:02:40,396
A setup guide, built in
Editor tools, profiles, modal editing, pets, fonts and terminal setup in one guide.

13
00:02:40,396 --> 00:02:47,379
Review before running
The terminal installer is prepared for review. It is not executed in this demo.

14
00:02:47,379 --> 00:02:51,892
A matching setup
Bundled wallpaper and profiles carry the Moonlight palette beyond the editor.

15
00:02:51,892 --> 00:02:59,922
Your workspace, your pace
Khonsu Moonlight 0.7.0  /  github.com/khons-hu/khonsu-moonlight  /  khns.dev
